{"message":{"container":null,"content":[{"text":"Looking at the buggy source, I can identify the issue:\n\n1. **The Bug**: The `negate` function simply returns `value` unchanged instead of implementing Boolean negation\n2. **The Fix**: It should return `Bool.not(value)` to properly negate the Boolean input\n\nThe law `negate_matches_boolean_not` requires that `negate(value) == Bool.not(value)` for all Bool values. The current implementation violates this because it doesn't actually negate anything.\n\n**Repair Strategy**:\n- Change the `negate` function body from `value` to `Bool.not(value)`\n- Keep the law and proof structure intact\n- The proof remains valid via the `{==}` reflexivity tactic since we're now directly implementing the required equivalence\n\n**Seeded Attack Rejection**:\nThe seeded attack SHA256 represents code that fails to implement total Boolean negation and thus violates the law. Any implementation that doesn't properly negate will fail the equality check required by the law.","type":"text"}],"context_management":null,"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011CfhnnmqYBEeMkCbS4DJpb","input_transformations":[],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":1626,"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"request_id":"req_011CfhnnmL2YzXwRKupaxRyt","session_id":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:59:58.867Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"14743177-0ca5-4da2-aef8-2104656ad088"}
